{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>For Heshbon is the city of Sihon king of the Amorites</b> — that is, now when Israel fought against him, the city of Sihon king of the Amorites it was, meaning the city of the king's residence. For <b>\"he fought against the king of Moab the first\"</b> — who reigned over them before a king [i.e., Sihon] ruled, or \"the first\" before Balak, who was king of Moab at that time. And Sihon took all his land from his hand as far as the Arnon. And Heshbon was at the beginning of the border of the conquest; therefore it is reckoned as belonging to the Amorite. And Israel was not warned concerning the land of Moab and the children of Ammon — only concerning the land that was in their possession at the time of the command. And Scripture brought proof that Heshbon is the city of Sihon, for the speakers say: <b>\"Come to Heshbon\"</b> etc., for at the time Sihon fought against the king of Moab, he first captured the city of Heshbon and the city was destroyed, and afterward he rebuilt it as a royal seat. And this is the meaning of <b>\"who dwells in Heshbon\"</b> (Numbers 21:34), and so it is stated in the book of Joshua (Joshua 13:10): <b>\"Sihon king of the Amorites, who reigned in Heshbon.\"</b> And the speakers would say to the Amorite: Come to Heshbon and dwell in it; let it be built and established after its destruction, O city of Sihon, whom you have set as king over it. And after Sihon dwelt in Heshbon, he gathered his forces there and conquered from the border of Moab as far as the Arnon, and the Arnon as well. Therefore the speakers said: <b>\"For a fire has gone out from Heshbon, a flame from the city of Sihon, who dwells in it, and it consumed Ar of Moab, the masters of the high places of the Arnon\"</b> — Sihon captured from Moab as far as the Arnon, and all the high places of the land and the masters of the high places, as in the matter of <b>\"and the high places of eternity for a possession\"</b> (Ezekiel 36:2). And he took additionally from the children of Ammon, from the Arnon as far as the Jabbok, as stated in Joshua (Joshua 13:24–25): <b>\"And Moses gave to the tribe of Gad…\"</b> <b>\"Jazer and all the cities of Gilead and half the land of the children of Ammon as far as Aroer\"</b> — and this is the land that the king of the children of Ammon was claiming from Jephthah, as he said: <b>\"Because Israel took my land from the Arnon as far as the Jabbok and as far as the Jordan\"</b> (Judges 11:13)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The verse quotations within the commentary preserve their bold lemma formatting where Ramban cites them as prooftexts; the canonical chapter:verse citations are normalized but were embedded parenthetically in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:37.488039499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}